  "summaries": {
    "en": "Transformation timing, spell cancels, and chapter-by-chapter boss routing for the critically acclaimed action game based on Journey to the West.",
    "ja": "変身タイミング、術キャンセル、章ごとのボス攻略ルートを整理。西遊記ベースの高評価アクションゲームを徹底解説。"
  },
  "category": "action",
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1538481199705-c710c4e965fc?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Cloud Step (invisible dodge) has no i-frames on entry but grants full invisibility for 3 seconds—use it to reposition, not to absorb attacks; entering while a hitbox is active still takes damage.",
      "Immobilise spell cancels boss attack animations on a 12-second cooldown. Apply it exclusively to the fastest boss combo starters (not mid-combo) to get the most punish time out of each cast.",
      "Staff Stances switch on the fly; Light Stance maximises combo speed, Pillar Stance deals the highest single-hit damage for stance breaks. Alternate Pillar R2 into Light combo loops against every boss with a visible stagger meter.",
      "Gourd charges (healing) are finite per bonfire rest. Count uses per chapter: Chapter 2 bosses deal roughly 30–40% of maximum HP per combo; entering with fewer than 4 Gourd charges is statistically a wipe.",
      "Secret bosses and optional paths require completing specific NPC quests in the same chapter—these expire at chapter end and cannot be recovered in New Game Plus without replaying from chapter select."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "筋斗雲（透明回避）は突入時に無敵フレームがなく、3秒間の完全不可視を与える。判定中に突入すればダメージを受けるため、攻撃吸収ではなく位置リセット目的で使う。",
      "金箍棒固め呪文はボスの攻撃アニメーションを12秒クールダウンで停止させる。コンボ中盤ではなく最速のコンボ始動技にのみ使い、反撃時間を最大化する。",
      "棍法は即座に切り替え可能。軽棍法はコンボ速度最優先、柱棍法はスタンス破壊の単発火力最高。全ボスを対象にスタンスメーターが見えたら柱R2から軽棍コンボループを繰り返す。",
      "葫芦チャージ（回復）は焚き火休憩ごとにリセットされる有限資源。第2章ボスはコンボ1回でHP最大値の30〜40%を削る。4チャージ以下での挑戦は統計的に全滅リスクが高い。",
      "隠しボスとオプションルートは同章内のNPCクエストを完了しないと出現せず、章終了で消滅する。NGPlusでも章セレクトで再プレイしない限り回収不能。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Chapter 1: Black Wind Mountain",
        "body": "Focus entirely on Staff Stance mastery before engaging the first major boss (Black Bear Guai). The game's tutorial deliberately under-explains Pillar Stance's stance-break role—enter the arena knowing that three Pillar Stance heavy attacks in sequence trigger a guaranteed stun. Collect the full complement of Gourd upgrades in the mountain exterior before the cave descent; two upgrades are missable after the cave seals."
      },
      {
        "title": "Spell Build Foundation",
        "body": "Prioritise the Immobilise and Rock Solid spell trees before offensive mind upgrades. Immobilise scales in duration with the Mind stat (from 2 seconds base to 5.5 seconds at Mind 15). Rock Solid's perfect parry window is 3 frames—visually cued by a golden flash on enemy attack wind-up, not the attack release. Mastering Rock Solid timing against non-boss enemies before attempting boss encounters significantly reduces Gourd consumption rates."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Chapter 3: The New West",
        "body": "Chapter 3 introduces the Yellow Wind Sage, whose sandstorm phase grounds all aerial attacks and reduces Immobilise duration to 1.5 seconds (from 3+). Switch to the Red Tides transformation (unlocked in Chapter 2) which grants sand immunity. The pre-boss preparation loop: collect Yellow Wind Spirit drops from common enemies in the chapter exterior for a passive resistance boost that stacks to 3 applications before the boss arena."
      },
      {
        "title": "Transformation Resource Management",
        "body": "Transformation meters (Qi) refill slowly in combat and quickly through perfect dodges. Each transformation has a 45-second cooldown after expiry; chaining two different transformations covers the cooldown of the first. Red Tides into Ancient Guanyin Temple is the most efficient 2-transformation chain: Red Tides for damage immunity during phase transitions and Ancient Guanyin for massive AoE stance break on boss recovery animations."
      },
      {
        "title": "Equipment Upgrade Path",
        "body": "Upgrade the Pilgrim's Staff to +5 before Chapter 4—it outperforms all Chapter 3 weapon drops until Chapter 5 due to its neutral scaling with both Strength and Spirit. Rings and headgear should prioritise Critical Hit Rate over flat damage: Wukong's critical hit multiplier at base is 1.75×, and each point of Crit Rate provides more expected DPS than equivalent flat damage investment past the 15% base threshold."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Chapter 6 Final Bosses",
        "body": "The Erlang Shen fight is the mechanical culmination of every system taught throughout the game. He uses all player abilities (Immobilise, Rock Solid, transformations) as counter-attacks when you cast spells. Counter-rotation: use Pillar Stance attacks to bait his Immobilise counter, then dodge out of his cast animation and punish his recovery. His third phase adds a 6-hit combo finisher—only block the first 3 hits and dodge the last 3 to avoid guard-break damage."
      },
      {
        "title": "True Ending Requirements",
        "body": "The true ending requires collecting all 6 headpieces from chapter-specific optional bosses. Three are missable on first playthrough due to NPC quest chains: the Spider Queen headpiece (Chapter 4), the Pale-Axe Stubborn Bull headpiece (Chapter 5), and the Gold-Scaled Python headpiece (Chapter 5 underground path). Use the chapter select from the Keeper's Shrine menu to replay missed chapters without restarting the game."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Using Cloud Step to dodge attacks rather than to reposition—Cloud Step has no invincibility frames on activation, meaning entering it inside an active hitbox deals full damage before invisibility takes effect.",
      "Hoarding Qi for transformations during normal combat—transformation cooldowns are shorter than the Qi regeneration rate outside boss encounters; use transformations freely in normal areas to maintain uptime.",
      "Skipping NPC interactions—most NPCs sell unique upgrade materials on first meeting that become unavailable after the chapter advances. Check every NPC shop on first encounter before moving forward.",
      "Attempting Secret Boss encounters without levelling Rock Solid to tier 3—Secret Bosses have attack speeds that invalidate raw dodge timing; Rock Solid perfect parries are mandatory, not optional, for no-death clears.",
      "Not duplicating Gourd charges before the final chapter—the Gourd limit increases with upgrade items found specifically in Chapter 5. Entering Chapter 6 with the base 4-charge Gourd instead of the maximum 9-charge version creates a significant survivability gap."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "筋斗雲を攻撃の回避ではなく位置リセットに使わない。発動時に無敵フレームがないため、判定中に使うと全ダメージを受けてから透明化する。",
      "通常戦闘で気功（変身ゲージ）を貯め続ける。変身クールダウンは通常戦闘での気功再生より短く、通常エリアでは積極的に使いアップタイムを稼ぐべき。",
      "NPCとの会話をスキップする。多くのNPCは初回会話時のみ固有強化素材を販売し、章進行後に消滅する。NPCショップは初見で必ず確認する。",
      "金剛禅（完璧受け流し）をティア3に強化せずに隠しボスに挑む。隠しボスの攻撃速度は素の回避タイミングを無効化し、完璧受け流しが必須となる。",
      "最終章前に葫芦チャージを増強しない。葫芦の最大チャージ数は第5章固有のアイテムで増加する。基本4チャージのまま第6章に入ると、最大9チャージとの生存率に大きな差が生まれる。"
    ]
  },
